---
import Layout from '@layouts/default.astro';
import Card from '@components/Card.astro';
import ContactPanel from '@components/ContactPanel.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Personal projects — Andrew Noblet"
  description="Explore the source of Andrew Noblet’s website, a working Angular island, and Web Component experiments."
>
  <div class="editorial-page">
    <section class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Personal projects</p><h1 class="editorial-title">
          Ideas you can<br />look inside.
        </h1><p>
          Small experiments and an evolving website. These examples show the
          code and interactions behind the presentation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-section">
      <div class="editorial-grid">
        <Card
          ><p class="eyebrow">01 / This website</p><h2>Astro portfolio</h2><p>
            A static website combining service pages, content collections,
            reusable components, and selected interactive islands. The
            repository shows the implementation and its development history.
          </p><a href="https://github.com/anoblet/astronautical-apogee"
            >Explore the source on GitHub →</a
          ></Card
        >
        <Card
          ><p class="eyebrow">02 / Framework integration</p><h2>
            Angular island
          </h2><p>
            A working Angular Material component rendered inside Astro. The
            increment interaction provides a small example of client hydration
            on a static page.
          </p><a href="/angular">Try the Angular demo →</a><a
            href="https://github.com/anoblet/astronautical-apogee/blob/main/src/components/angular/material-demo.component.ts"
            >View the component source →</a
          ></Card
        >
        <Card
          ><p class="eyebrow">03 / Web Components</p><h2>Lit components</h2><p>
            The website’s appearance controls use Lit. Explore a small component
            page and browse the implementation of the shared controls.
          </p><a href="/lit">Explore the Lit page →</a><a
            href="https://github.com/anoblet/astronautical-apogee/tree/main/src/components"
            >Browse component source →</a
          ></Card
        >
        <Card
          ><p class="eyebrow">04 / Development workflows</p><h2>
            Automation experiments
          </h2><p>
            Experiments with scripting and AI-assisted workflows are part of how
            I explore repetitive development work. Read the notes and inspect
            the repository rather than treating a tool description as a finished
            product.
          </p><a href="/blog/genaiscript-usage">Read the workflow notes →</a
          ></Card
        >
      </div>
    </section>
    <ContactPanel />
  </div>
</Layout>
